  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Women in Informal Cross Border trade in Great lakes region (EWICBT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to social economic empowerment of women in cross border trade between Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) and Rwanda. This will be achieved through improving their business environment and increasing their income and their social economic welfare. To accomplish this, the project is built on improving the legal and policy framework for WICBT, providing access to legal aid services to WICBT, increasing WICBT&#x2019;s access to Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights and strengthen the entrepreneurial and financial capacity of WICBT.
The overall objective of this project is to contribute to social economic empowerment of women in cross border trade between DRC and Rwanda. The specific objectives are the following: 
Objective 1:  To improve the legal and policy framework for WICBT 
To achieve this objective WICBT and stakeholders will be provided with simplified and translated laws and capacitated to influence laws and policies that affect (Women Informal Cross Border Traders) WICBTs and Advocacy activities to improve the trade environment of women in ICBT will be conducted.  
Objective 2: To provide access to legal aid services to WICBT
This objective aims at addressing the existing lack of legal service support to women who are harassed, sexually abused and their goods confiscated in their transactions 
Objective 3: To increase WICBT&#x2019;s access to Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights
The project intends to raise awareness, equip (Women Informal Cross Border Traders) WICBT with skills to take informed decision on control of their body, engage their husband and link their families with SRHR service providers.   
Objective 4: To strengthen the entrepreneurial and financial capacity of WICBT 
This objective aims at contributing and sustaining overall economic empowerment of (Women Informal Cross Border Traders) WICBT in Rwanda and DRC. It focuses on strengthening their capacity to bridge gaps in financial literacy, working with financial institutions, increasing their capabilities in the entrepreneurial development and cooperatives management.</narrative>
  </description>
